Hi Simon,

[2015-01-06 18:37] Brown, Simon wrote:
> Hello list.  I have just started using eclipse+StatET today in a linux environment.
>
> Installation and setup has gone fairly smoothly, with most of the
> challenge coming from getting my head round eclipse.
>
> One problem I have not been able to find a solution for is being able
> to load data files from the project directory.  I can do so if I
> explicitly set the whole path.  Eg
> This works:  load('/home/user/dir1/dir2/project_dir/data_file.Rsave')
> This does not: load('data_file.Rsave')
>
> Outside of eclipse this works fine.  So it seems that the environment
> is not picking up the pwd, or '.', directory as being the first entry
> in the path.  This may be due to the project not being in the default
> workspace location.
>
> Any ideas on how to set this right?

You can configure the initial working directory for R in the launch 
configuration of your R console in StatET.

You can set it to the complete path:
     /home/user/dir1/dir2/<project_dir>

Or specify it by using Eclipse variables, e.g. for a specific project:
     ${project_loc:<project_name>}

Regards,
Stephan

